Title:
ADWS LDAP Beacon Object File (ADWS-BOF)

Type:
GitHub Tool

Short Summary (4-8 sentences max):
- This repository provides a Cobalt Strike Beacon Object File (BOF) that performs LDAP queries via Active Directory Web Services (ADWS) instead of direct LDAP.  
- It enables operators to run LDAP searches using either the current Beacon access token (SSPI/implicit auth) or explicit domain credentials supplied on the command line.  
- The BOF supports specifying the LDAP filter, base DN, and returned attributes, and can automatically resolve the Domain Controller IP (with an override via `--ip`).  
- It’s useful for red teams/pentesters who want AD enumeration through ADWS (TCP/9389) in environments where classic LDAP paths/controls are constrained or monitored differently.  
- The implementation is a C BOF-compatible adaptation inspired by/leveraging concepts from ZakiPedio’s BridgeHead library, and is explicitly marked as work-in-progress with planned enhancements (output formatting, BH JSON conversion, and potential AD abuse helpers like RBCD workflows).

Technical Focus:
- ADWS (Active Directory Web Services) LDAP querying over TCP/9389
- Cobalt Strike BOF development (C, Beacon integration)
- Authentication via current access token vs supplied credentials
- LDAP search parameters: filter, base DN, attribute selection
- Domain Controller discovery / auto-resolution logic

Use Cases:
- AD user/group/computer enumeration from Beacon without using standard LDAP tooling
- Querying nested group membership using matching rule OID `1.2.840.113556.1.4.1941`
- Operating in networks where LDAP (389/636) is restricted but ADWS is reachable
- Running LDAP queries under the context of an impersonated token in Beacon
- Building operator workflows for AD data collection and later ingestion (e.g., BloodHound-style pipelines)

Keywords:
ADWS, Active Directory Web Services, LDAP, TCP 9389, Cobalt Strike, Beacon Object File, BOF, SSPI, access token, domain controller discovery, LDAP filter, base DN, attributes, 1.2.840.113556.1.4.1941, nested group membership, Windows Active Directory, BridgeHead, red team enumeration, CNA script